[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119854,
      "id": "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe",
      "title": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1e85a204-e096-567a-8b8a-7f1cd5f9d568",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\na_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_3=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b,$ then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+x_2\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+x_3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 3 x_{1} \\\\ - 2 x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}- 3 x_{2} \\\\ - 8 x_{2} \\\\ 6 x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 x_{3} \\\\ 5 x_{3} \\\\ - 3 x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} - 3 x_{2} + 2 x_{3} \\\\ 3 x_{1} - 8 x_{2} + 5 x_{3} \\\\ - 2 x_{1} + 6 x_{2} - 3 x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - 3 x_{2} + 2 x_{3} &=6 \\\\ 3 x_{1} - 8 x_{2} + 5 x_{3} &=16 \\\\ - 2 x_{1} + 6 x_{2} - 3 x_{3} &=-13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 16 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & -13\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M&=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 16 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & -13\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & -13\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-3)R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(2)R_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - 3 x_{2} + 2 x_{3} &=6 \\\\ x_{2} - x_{3} &=-2 \\\\ x_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n1x_2+(-1)(-1)=-2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2=-3\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1+(-3)(-3)+(2)(-1)=6\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1=-1\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is $x_1=-1$, $x_2=-3$, $x_3=-1$, which means\n\n$$\n-1a_1+(-3)a_2+(-1)a_3=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}=(-1)+(-3)+(-1)=-5.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
