  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119854,
      "id": "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe",
      "title": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ff57d944-2359-579f-87a1-a6a3e226c177",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\na_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_3=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b,$ then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+x_2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+x_3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}- x_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ - x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 x_{3} \\\\ 5 x_{3} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} - x_{2} + 2 x_{3} \\\\ 5 x_{3} \\\\ 3 x_{1} - x_{2} + x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - x_{2} + 2 x_{3} &=0 \\\\ 5 x_{3} &=-5 \\\\ 3 x_{1} - x_{2} + x_{3} &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M&=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-3)R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -5\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -5\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}:=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - x_{2} + 2 x_{3} &=0 \\\\ x_{2} - \\frac{5 x_{3}}{2} &=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ x_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n1x_2+\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)(-1)=\\frac{9}{2}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2=2\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1+(-1)(2)+(2)(-1)=0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1=4\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is $x_1=4$, $x_2=2$, $x_3=-1$, which means\n\n$$\n4a_1+(2)a_2+(-1)a_3=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}=(4)+(2)+(-1)=5.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "425ca376-c50b-545a-ae61-6329eea55033",
