  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119854,
      "id": "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe",
      "title": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bc767ab3-7ed6-5983-a575-3f03a72ccf16",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\na_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_2=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_3=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad b=\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b,$ then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+x_2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+x_3\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ 3 x_{2} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 x_{3} \\\\ 3 x_{3} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} \\\\ 3 x_{2} + 3 x_{3} \\\\ x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}21 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} &=21 \\\\ 3 x_{2} + 3 x_{3} &=27 \\\\ x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3} &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 15\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M&=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 15\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-1)R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}:=\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} &=21 \\\\ x_{2} + x_{3} &=9 \\\\ x_{3} &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=3.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n1x_2+(1)(3)=9\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2=6\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1+(1)(6)+(3)(3)=21\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1=6\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is $x_1=6$, $x_2=6$, $x_3=3$, which means\n\n$$\n6a_1+(6)a_2+(3)a_3=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3}=(6)+(6)+(-3)=9.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
