  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119854,
      "id": "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe",
      "title": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1044e2dd-3da8-5eeb-8969-7878d92e8d90",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\na_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_2=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_3=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b,$ then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+x_2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+x_3\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ - 2 x_{2} \\\\ 2 x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 x_{3} \\\\ - 11 x_{3} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} \\\\ - 2 x_{2} - 11 x_{3} \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} + x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} &=4 \\\\ - 2 x_{2} - 11 x_{3} &=4 \\\\ x_{1} + 2 x_{2} + x_{3} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M&=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-1)R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & 4\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & 0\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(2)R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=\\left(- \\frac{1}{15}\\right)R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} + x_{2} + 3 x_{3} &=4 \\\\ x_{2} - 2 x_{3} &=-2 \\\\ x_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=0.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n1x_2+(-2)(0)=-2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2=-2\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1+(1)(-2)+(3)(0)=4\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1=6\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is $x_1=6$, $x_2=-2$, $x_3=0$, which means\n\n$$\n6a_1+(-2)a_2+(0)a_3=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}=(6)+(-2)+(0)=4.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
