  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119854,
      "id": "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe",
      "title": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fe165a72-c778-5239-b131-dcf60892fb8c",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\na_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad a_3=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad b=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 30 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b,$ then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If $x_1a_1+x_2a_2+x_3a_3=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+x_2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+x_3\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 30 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}- x_{2} \\\\ 5 x_{2} \\\\ 2 x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ x_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 30 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} - x_{2} \\\\ 5 x_{2} + x_{3} \\\\ 3 x_{1} + 2 x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}&=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 30 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - x_{2} &=-11 \\\\ 5 x_{2} + x_{3} &=30 \\\\ 3 x_{1} + 2 x_{2} &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 30 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M&=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 30 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 30 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 25\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-3)R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 30 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-1)R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{5} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] && R_{2}:=\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{5} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right] && R_{3}:=(-1)R_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1} - x_{2} &=-11 \\\\ x_{2} + \\frac{x_{3}}{5} &=6 \\\\ x_{3} &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=5.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n1x_2+\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)(5)=6\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2=5\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1+(-1)(5)+(0)(5)=-11\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1=-6\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is $x_1=-6$, $x_2=5$, $x_3=5$, which means\n\n$$\n-6a_1+(5)a_2+(5)a_3=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}=(-6)+(5)+(5)=4.\n$$\n\n",
